WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
One French sentence: «Actuellement,
la librairie propose une formation

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.070
gratuite.» Three words in
it look just like English.

3
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.830
Do they mean what you think?

4
00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.070
Next, a short story from
1884 slips in the words

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.960
«comme par une erreur du destin».

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.680
Now add 30 questions, 40 minutes,

7
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.610
and four kinds of text.

8
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.770
So how do you read an ad,

9
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.260
an article and a novel page for
exactly what each question asks?

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.900
In this mission, you'll
map the four text types

11
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.690
on a 40-minute bar.

12
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.940
Then you'll take on a
flyer headed «Atelier BD»,

13
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.430
and track down every condition on it.

14
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.220
Your mission: find out
how to read each kind

15
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.270
of text for what the questions want.
